# pokemon_le 0.82 - Spike 3 (64-bit ARM): drafted by s3port.py (PAD-1287) from the Spike 3 port star_wars_elg-1.10.port (star_wars_elg 1.10).
# Functions paired across the two titles: 9333 of 18297 reference functions (7783 anchored by vtable slots and strings, 361 through calls that line up, the rest grown through calls); half of them line up 100% or better.
# Written: what the reference port carries that is the FRAMEWORK's (each site's function at least 75% alike its
# reference's, each global and offset read at the lined-up instruction, the engines' layouts re-read off this program's
# own code); the switch lines from this program's own device table. The reference game's own content (shows, lamps,
# callouts, scenes, held coils, its modes) is not this title's: written as comments, for its own port.
# Emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1289) on the Spike 3 rig (tools/spike3_emu/proofs/s3proof.sh TITLE=pokemon_le, slot 129,
# hidden, muted, prebuilt/mode64.so): the runtime took this port whole (29 sites, 45 shots), held back the Insider
# achievement query (type 28), armed the 6 events with the dispatch hooked and both switch_hit sites. POKE TEST (a mode
# file: trigger 0x80 x3, 20 s, shots 0x8000140000) started on the third Berry target left hit (switch 36), scored 6
# shots through the game's score_add (+21,000,000: score 1,350 -> 22,891,120) and ended when its 20 s ran out.
# Program sha1 36560010984f742b74fb8e582f7465c76e852e3d (games/game).
# Ball save emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1289, PROOF=ballsave): SAVE TEST's 15 s save through multiball_serve, the drain
# 3 s in served back (trough eject, auto plunger), 3 shots scored on that ball, the drain after the save ended it; the
# control (no ball_save) ended the ball on its first drain. Multiball (PROOF=mb): a mode file's `multiball 3 10` had the
# game serve 3 balls (trough 3/6), counted 3 -> 2, ended on its clock and gave the game its multiball back at one ball.
# Written card (PAD-1289): the app's Write put a BERRY RUSH mode on a copy of the library card; booted on the rig its own
# hook started the game with this port (/games/pad/padmode/game.port), the mode started on the third Berry target left
# hit, scored 5 shots (+15,000,000) and ended on its 20 s clock; its modes read back off the card whole.
# Switch ids are the game's own: its device table's names are UTF-8 (a "POKÉ BALL SPOT" record had cut the walk, every
# id 16 low, before PAD-1289). Not carried: the game's own modes, shows, lamps, callouts and scenes, for later work.

game           pokemon_le
version        0.82

